{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1456397-red-talons-in-earthblood","id":1456397,"title":"Red Talons in Earthblood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-09T01:52:05-07:00","id":1456397,"title":"Red Talons in Earthblood","content":"Hello guys, despite the fact I'm one of the few persons who actually really enjoy Earthblood's plot, setting and atmosphere, (I found it really grim and desperate, as I like my chronicles),<br /> I was wondering if anyone else has noticed something about Onawa and the Red Talons<br /> <br /> <br /> SPOILER ALERT<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">When Cahal frees Onawa, she says that she's the leader of the Red Talons. If you talk with her, Cahal says ''I've heard about the red talons, most of them are born from wolf, not from humans'', and Onawa says that she was born Uktena and then adopted.<br /> From the white wolf Wikia</div></div> </div> </div></span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>'Cahal learns about their research and frees a captured Red Talon that Endron has been experimenting on, Onawa''</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Can this be a major plot twist for the Red Talons? Homid Red Talons who refuse everything that is human, much like Predator Kings from forsaken? What's your opinion?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">I think that realistically it could have sense, since the tribe should be almost wiped out, otherwise. On the other hand, it's a major change, which it seems very invasive.</span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T04:02:01-07:00","id":1456404,"title":"","content":"Yeah.........Earthbound was....interesting. Basically unless Griffon changes it mind thats a non-starter, and as Griffin is among the most stubborn Incarna in existence I don't see that happening. Earthbound was based on someones home game and it seems to have incorporated a lot of their ' house rules' into the bargain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T04:04:56-07:00","id":1456405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1456397-red-talons-in-earthblood?p=1456404#post1456404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah.........Earthbound was....interesting. Basically unless Griffon changes it mind thats a non-starter, and as Griffin is among the most stubborn Incarna in existence I don't see that happening. Earthbound was based on someones home game and it seems to have incorporated a lot of their ' house rules' into the bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Earthblood based on homerules ? Why are you saying so ? Are there any interwievs or sources ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T04:07:54-07:00","id":1456406,"title":"","content":"Animal experimentation is far more common than that in humans, so I fail to see - at least without knowing any more details of the game that might imply otherwise - how being imprisoned in a lab leads to the notion of Onawa being Homid instead of, a Lupus of the Uktena that left its tribe to join the Talons out of dissatisfaction with a dominance of Homid perspective in their dealing with the Wyrm and humanity, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-22-2021, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://fo