curious about what really went on with the writing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><i>''I was born Uktena. The Red Talons took me when I was just a girl. They dragged me to their caern to kill me</i></b> '' Then she explains that the Caern spirit created a connection with her.<br /> <br /> ''I heard stories about the red talons and their closeness to nature. Most of them are born from wolves, not humans''<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T06:15:34-07:00","id":1456422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1456397-red-talons-in-earthblood?p=1456418#post1456418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><i>''I was born Uktena. The Red Talons took me when I was just a girl. They dragged me to their caern to kill me</i></b> '' Then she explains that the Caern spirit created a connection with her.<br /> <br /> ''I heard stories about the red talons and their closeness to nature. Most of them are born from wolves, not humans''<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh boy, 100% &quot;kick the lore in the face&quot; country. If you're going to go so blatantly against the current of canon/fanon, at least have the decency of doing some lampshade hanging. You just embarass yourselves with the fanbase otherwise.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Question - what kind of role do the Talons play or not in the game's narrative. Because unless they are <b><i>meant </i></b>to be unsympathetic and major (or at least mid-level) antagonists, that whole little personal story was a <b><i>completely </i></b>unnecessary shock value piece. The Talons take more than enough crap from lore &amp; metaplot already.<br /> <br /> Ok, it might <b>not </b>be completely absurd if it was a &quot;Talons decide to sacrifice some human kid because, <i>curse humans too much of your kind upon our beloved Gaia already</i>&quot; and midway through their bringing the little girl into the caern its totem - that would definitely be anything <b>but</b> Griffin - notices the child is a budding Garou and intervenes because unknowingly sacrificing a brethren, even if Homid, is too much. And maybe imposes the adoption upon the Talons as penance for their sloppy (&quot;Seriously, even if you hadn't c<i>ompletely bungled things by <b>not noticing you picked a homid cub instead of a human</b></i> for sacrifice already - why some Uktena kinfolk kid and not a farm manager or some suited worm stinking of all kinds of weird human oils, are you hypocrites, cowards or just utter idiots?!&quot;) sacrifice selection.<br /> <br /> All of that said, maybe <i>a little</i> too unique of a personal history, depending on how major or minor a role Onawa has or not in the game's narrative, imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-22-2021, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T06:27:11-07:00","id":1456424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1456397-red-talons-in-earthblood?p=1456405#post1456405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Earthblood based on homerules ? Why are you saying so ? Are there any interwievs or sources ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Theres an interview somewhere ( I read it over a year ago so I don't remember where.) with one of the developers stating that Cahal was based on their old character and that other npcs in the game were somewhat based on other PCs, so it wouldn't suprise me if other details from the home game found their way in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T06:27:43-07:00","id":1456425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1456397-red-talons-in-earthblood?p=1456422#post1456422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh boy, 100% &quot;kick the lore in the face&quot; country. If you're going to go so blatantly against the current of canon/fanon, at least have the decency of doing some lampshade hanging. You just embarass yourselves with the fanbase otherwise.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Question - what kind of role do the Talons play or not in the game's narrative. Because unless they are <b><i>meant </i></b>to be unsympathetic and major (or at least mid-level) antagonists, that whole little personal story was <b><i>completely </i></b>unnecessary shock value piece. The Talons take more than enough crap from lore &amp; metaplot already.<br /> <br /> Ok, it might <b>not </b>be completely absurd if it was a &quot;Talons decide to sacrifice some human kid because, <i>curse humans too much of your kind upon our beloved Gaia already</i>&quot; and midway through their bringing the little girl into the caern its totem - that would definitely be anything <b>but</b> Griffin - notices the child is a budding Garou and intervenes because unknowingly sacrificing a brethren, even if Homid, is too much. And maybe imposes the adoption upon the Talons as penance for their sloppy (&quot;Seriously, even if you hadn't c<i>ompletely bungled things by <b>not noticing you picked a homid cub instead of a human</b></i> for sacrifice already - why some Uktena kinfolk kid and not a farm manager or some suited worm stinking of all kinds of weird human oils, are you hypocrites, cowards or just utter idiots?!&quot;) sacrifice selection.<br /> <br /> All of that said, maybe a little too unique a personal history, depending on how major or minor a role Onawa has or not in the game's narrative, imho.</div> </div> </div> </div>I overall agree with you on your analisis.<br /> <br /> But now you kow why I opened this thread, in the game, as you see, the words are pretty clear.<br /> The thing about Onawa, is that you can only discover what I quoted, and no more, no details on the attempted murder, or anything else, so it's very character-fluff.<br /> I'm ok with Red Talons killing innocents, even random (I mean, just read the story on the revised book), because it's part of their tragedy, and because I like 1-2nd edition more, where many garou were openly almost bad guys and zealots, and also, as in Earthblood, they can show the more radical and brutal culture of some tribes, and the consequences of it. But Onawa's background should have been examinated a bit more. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T08:18:32-07:00","id":1456432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1456397-red-talons-in-earthblood?p=1456425#post1456425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I overall agree with you on your analisis.<br /> <br /> But now you kow why I opened this thread, in the game, as you see, the words are pretty clear.<br /> The thing about Onawa, is that you can only discover what I quoted, and no more, no details on the attempted murder, or anything else, so it's very character-fluff.<br /> I'm ok with Red Talons killing innocents, even random (I mean, just read the story on the revised book), because it's part of their tragedy, and because I like 1-2nd edition more, where many garou were openly almost bad guys and zealots, and also, as in Earthblood, they can show the more radical and brutal culture of some tribes, and the consequences of it. But Onawa's background should have been examinated a bit more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not against in the least to Garou being shown at times as brutal, vicious and somewhat in the wrong due to the horrid mix of animalistic primal rage with all too human ideological zealotry.<br /> It's the gratuitously mean and wall-banging idiotic portrayal of the Red Talons we get from the whole &quot;let's sacrifice a random kinfolk of another tribe...oh wait, it's an actual budding garou, oops&quot; setup i take issue with.<br /> <br /> You want to do edgy horror/shock <b>and </b>surprise the fanbase, go for Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, Fianna or Glass Walkers killing a whole schoolbus of technical students, Silver Fangs going &quot;mindwhammy then impregnate&quot; in dozens of young socialites or ladies of aristocratic upbringing, other tribes filching Silver Fangs of &quot;inadequate lineage&quot; or what have you. Make it bad, ugly but logical in a twisted sort of way.<br /> <br /> Using a tribe that <i><b>already </b></i>gets the &quot;almost card-carrying villain&quot; stick 9 times out of 10 in the books (alongside the Get of Fenris and Shadow Lords) to do that super-bungled sacrifice scenario, doesn't really cut it for me. <i>Specially </i>if it serves no narrative function in the game's plot to throw the Talons in such an unflattering light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-20-2021, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T08:25:07-07:00","id":1456434,"title":"","content":"Human sacrifice of this variety was almost entirely retconned into a Dying Cubs thing in Revised, and the Dying Cubs wouldn't let any witnesses leave, because they're rather sus to the rest of the tribe, to say nothing of the rest of the Garou Nation. This is wallowing in some early-edition &quot;Yuletide Rites&quot; material that doesn't utilize the concept of the Talons to any quality end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T09:29:50-07:00","id":1456437,"title":"","content":"Anyway, let me stop derailing the thread - by railing on a scene of a game i never played, to boot - and try to explore the kernel of an idea Helur asked about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Could Red Talons secretly adopt Homids and brainwash them into </i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><i>refuse everything that is human in their origins</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> The tribe as whole, definitely not, because most might see this as a sort of betrayal even without Griffin possibly getting pissed with the idea.<br /> But <b><i>individual </i></b>septs with <i><b>other </b></i>totems, specially ones with an element of trickery, might be amenable to the idea of <i>purifying</i> any Homid foundlings or lost cubs they come across in their travels or strikes against human pollution-producing businesses.<br /> <br /> Giving them a (reverse?) Mowgli treatment of sorts of <b><i>taking the man out</i></b> the children of kinfolk families, Black Spiral, lost cubs or other (Director Alreed from Pentex was of Get of Fenris stock and Samuel Haight descends from either Children of Gaia or Fianna, if memory tricks me not), as a step towards purificating humanity and herding it toward a more nature harmonic path instead of straight genocide.<br /> <br /> Damn, considering how messed up with all kinds of mental issues even non-fomor working on Pentex can be, kids being taken from such families might <i><b>welcome </b></i>&quot;going wild child&quot; alongside the Talons, even those who never become Garou. It might even be a more <i><b>compassionate </b></i>destiny - at least from a Talon perspective, if no one else's, in dealing with Humanity and the Weaver &amp; Wyrm's influence in their society as a whole.<br /> <br /> Yes, i think it could work as some sort of weird secret society kind of heretical camp within the tribe, like the Society of Nidhogg for Shadow Lords - except not as moustache-twirling apocalyptic doomsday cult villains like the Society, that is. Damn, the &quot;Mowgli Herders&quot; might even be said to be sort of wholesome for Talons, i guess.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-09-2021, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T10:52:50-07:00","id":1456441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1456397-red-talons-in-earthblood?p=1456437#post1456437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, let me stop derailing the thread - by railing on a scene of a game i never played, to boot - and try to explore the kernel of an idea Helur asked about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Could Red Talons secretly adopt Homids and brainwash them into </i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><i>refuse everything that is human in their origins</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> The tribe as whole, definitely not, because most might see this as a sort of betrayal even without Griffin possibly getting pissed with the idea.<br /> But <b><i>individual </i></b>septs with <i><b>other </b></i>totems, specially ones with an element of trickery, might be amenable to the idea of <i>purifying</i> any Homid foundlings or lost cubs they come across in their travels or strikes against human pollution-producing businesses.<br /> <br /> Giving them a (reverse?) Mowgli treatment of sorts of <b><i>taking the man out</i></b> the children of kinfolk families, Black Spiral, lost cubs or other (Director Alreed from Pentex was of Get of Fenris stock and Samuel Haight descends from either Children of Gaia or Fianna, if memory tricks me not), as a step towards purificating humanity and herding it toward a more nature harmonic path instead of straight genocide.<br /> <br /> Damn, considering how messed up with all kinds of mental issues even non-fomor working on Pentex can be, kids being taken from such families might <i><b>welcome </b></i>&quot;going wild child&quot; alongside the Talons, even those who never become Garou. It might even be a more <i><b>compassionate </b></i>destiny - at least from a Talon perspective, if no one else's, in dealing with Humanity and the Weaver &amp; Wyrm's influence in their society as a whole.<br /> <br /> Yes, i think it could work as some sort of weird secret society kind of heretical camp within the tribe, like the Society of Nidhogg for Shadow Lords - except not as moustache-twirling apocalyptic doomsday cult villains like the Society, that is. Damn, the &quot;Mowgli Herders&quot; might even be said to be sort of wholesome for Talons, i guess.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this kind of idea, or similar, regarding a secret camp of Red Talons ''rewilding'' humans or offer place to homid garou who are devoured by hate for humanity, on the edge of harano or worse, in exchange of their human lifestyle, could be a solid base for some intriguing evolution in w5 timeline. <br /> Honestly, I'm a fan of ''red talons go only lupus'' , by the way, I really don't know how the tribe could survive modern era, and I'm not talking about deforestation or killing of wolves or their numbers, but also about their mental health and balance. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T12:02:51-07:00","id":1456445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1456397-red-talons-in-earthblood?p=1456441#post1456441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that this kind of idea, or similar, regarding a secret camp of Red Talons ''rewilding'' humans or offer place to homid garou who are devoured by hate for humanity, on the edge of harano or worse, in exchange of their human lifestyle, could be a solid base for some intriguing evolution in w5 timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely open rooms for some intriguing story possibilities and a venue for unexpectedly social/political plotlines centered on the Red Talons, what can be a plus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1456397-red-talons-in-earthblood?p=1456441#post1456441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'm a fan of ''red talons go only lupus'' , by the way, I really don't know how the tribe could survive modern era, and I'm not talking about deforestation or killing of wolves or their numbers, but also about their mental health and balance.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Glass Walkers are almost the opposite breed-wise and without meaning too, so there might be a balance of the imbalanced there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But Lupus do have one major two-edged difference in relation to Homids: Turning adult in 2-3 years like wolves, instead of 15-20 like humans. That combined with litters could provide some scary advantage for a warmongering Lupus with a good head for numbers and a good starting base wolf kinfolk packs for breeding.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or some wacko ronin deciding to make itself into the &quot;Wolf Shogun&quot; or somesuch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-09-2021, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T07:11:39-07:00","id":1456661,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I mean, the Red Talon caern's spirits are complaining that the Talons don't care about them. Which, given the 5 gnosis of your basic lupus, is kinda confusing.<br /> <br /> I feel the whole Talon/Onawa thing was to show an antagonistic garou faction.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 08-12-2021, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T22:09:10-07:00","id":1456738,"title":"","content":"The Red Talons felt a little out-of-character. And no, I know tribes are not stereotypes BUT...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T13:25:43-07:00","id":1457048,"title":"","content":"Red Talons Revised mentions that a homid Talon is a sign of the apocalypse and a unique event. Onowa could be that if you want to tie if to something &quot;canon&quot;. However, I believe this was just a factor of them streamlining things and wanted to avoid introducing too many tribes or concepts at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/918-geeklord1","name":"geeklord1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar918_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}